# Copy to bot_service_update.conf (same folder) ONLY on a client server
# whose defaults need to differ from the standard ones. This file is
# plain bash - it's sourced directly by setup_officer_bot.sh.
#
# Leave it absent entirely on a normal India-based client - the script's
# built-in defaults (TEMPLATE_DIR=otm_whatsapp_group_bot_service,
# BASE_PORT=8732, DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CODE=91) are correct as-is.

# TEMPLATE_DIR="otm_whatsapp_group_bot_service"   # only if this client names it differently
# BASE_PORT=8740                                   # only if 8732+ is already used by something else
# DEFAULT_COUNTRY_CODE=971                         # e.g. a UAE-based client

# NODE_BIN_OVERRIDE: only needed if the script's auto-detection (it scans
# common nvm install folders for the newest Node found) picks the wrong
# binary on this server. Set this to the exact output of, on this server:
#   readlink -f $(which node)
# Example (this server, confirmed 2026-09-30):
# NODE_BIN_OVERRIDE="/root/.nvm/versions/node/v20.20.2/bin/node"

# ODOO_INBOUND_URL: only set this if you want the optional reply chatbot
# (otm_whatsapp_lead_scheduler > WhatsApp > Configuration > Lead Scheduler
# Settings > Enable Reply Chatbot) to work. Every NEW officer instance
# created after you set this will have it written into its own .env
# automatically - existing instances need it added to their .env by hand
# (then `pm2 restart <name>`) since this script never touches an existing
# instance's files.
# ODOO_INBOUND_URL="https://erp.elysians360.in/otm_whatsapp_lead/inbound"
